      "pos_start_est": 414
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": "wang2022deepnet",
      "n_tokens_est": 1,
      "pos_start_est": 416
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": ", but equipping them with longer context remains difficult",
      "n_tokens_est": 9,
      "pos_start_est": 417
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "markup",
      "text": "~",
      "n_tokens_est": 1,
      "pos_start_est": 426
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "markup",
      "text": "\\citep",
      "n_tokens_est": 2,
      "pos_start_est": 427
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": "tay2020long",
      "n_tokens_est": 1,
      "pos_start_est": 429
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": ", since the self-attention module at their heart has time and memory complexity quadratic in sequence length. An important question is whether making attention faster and more memory-efficient can help Transformer models address their runtime and memory challenges for long sequences. Many approximate attention methods have aimed to reduce the compute and memory requirements of attention. These methods range from sparse-approximation",
      "n_tokens_est": 70,
      "pos_start_est": 430
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "markup",
      "text": "~",
      "n_tokens_est": 1,
      "pos_start_est": 500
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "markup",
      "text": "\\citep",
      "n_tokens_est": 2,
      "pos_start_est": 501
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": "kitaev2020reformer, roy2021efficient",
      "n_tokens_est": 3,
      "pos_start_est": 503
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": " to low-rank approximation",
      "n_tokens_est": 5,
      "pos_start_est": 506
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "markup",
      "text": "~",
      "n_tokens_est": 1,
      "pos_start_est": 511
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "markup",
      "text": "\\citep",
      "n_tokens_est": 2,
      "pos_start_est": 512
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": "wang2020linformer, katharopoulos2020transformers, choromanski2020rethinking",
      "n_tokens_est": 5,
      "pos_start_est": 514
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": ", and their combinations",
      "n_tokens_est": 4,
      "pos_start_est": 519
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "markup",
      "text": "~",
      "n_tokens_est": 1,
      "pos_start_est": 523
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "markup",
      "text": "\\citep",
      "n_tokens_est": 2,
      "pos_start_est": 524
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": "beltagy2020longformer, zaheer2020bigbird, scatterbrain",
      "n_tokens_est": 5,
      "pos_start_est": 526
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": ". Although these methods reduce the compute requirements to linear or near-linear in sequence length, many of them do not display wall-clock speedup against standard attention and have not gained wide adoption. One main reason is that they focus on FLOP reduction (which may not correlate with wall-clock speed) and tend to ignore overheads from memory access (IO). In this paper, we argue that a missing principle is making attention algorithms ",
      "n_tokens_est": 85,
      "pos_start_est": 531
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "markup",
      "text": "\\textit",
      "n_tokens_est": 2,
      "pos_start_est": 616
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": "IO-aware",
      "n_tokens_est": 3,
      "pos_start_est": 618
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "markup",
      "text": "~",
      "n_tokens_est": 1,
      "pos_start_est": 621
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "markup",
      "text": "\\citep",
      "n_tokens_est": 2,
      "pos_start_est": 622
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": "aggarwal1988input",
      "n_tokens_est": 1,
      "pos_start_est": 624
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "markup",
      "text": "---",
      "n_tokens_est": 3,
      "pos_start_est": 625
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": "that is, carefully accounting for reads and writes to different levels of fast and slow memory (e.g., between fast GPU on-chip SRAM and relatively slow GPU high bandwidth memory, or HBM",
      "n_tokens_est": 40,
      "pos_start_est": 628
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
